# core/data/talk/grammar/en/surf_a_third.tlk - more replies when the player takes part in a row between
# others: accuse, defend, take a side, mediate (owner: TK; T5b package T5B-SURF1, Surface push A).
# Content only. Clean in any room: nobody is hurt, nothing is aimed at a child, no blame reply (the
# cool banks are not touched), no register word, no romance. Kid voices are kid banks. Rule names start
# with sa_. Syntax: talkc_gen.py.

# ---- ACCUSE: "it was them" ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.accuse.sa_disagree act: disagree
  "Me, never, I was nowhere near it. I have a witness. A good one."
  "Hold on, that's a big word, accuse. Do you have a receipt?"
  "I'd never, ask anyone. Well, don't ask the cat. She knows."
  "That's a serious charge. I want my lawyer, a sandwich and a nap."
  "Not me, check the evidence. The evidence is a crumb. Check it."
  "Oh, you've got the wrong person. Try again, with less pointing."
  "Pointing fingers is rude. And my finger's shorter. Think about that."
  "No, no, no, I was elsewhere. Possibly asleep. Hard to prove."
@rule core.accuse.sa_disagree_topic guard: topic act: disagree
  "Me and {x}? You've got it backwards. {x:cap} did it to me."
  "Leave {x} out of it. It's innocent. I'd bet my hat on it."
  "If it's about {x}, I'm completely innocent. Ask the neighbours."
@rule core.accuse.sa_disagree_blunt guard: blunt act: disagree
  "Nope. Wasn't me. You're pointing at the wrong thing."
  "Wrong. Next accusation, please. Try one that's true."
@rule core.accuse.sa_disagree_polite guard: polite act: disagree
  "I'm afraid there's been a misunderstanding. I should never."
  "With respect, I'd like to correct the record. It wasn't me."
@rule core.accuse.sa_disagree_elder guard: elder act: disagree
  "In my day, we waited for the facts. Facts first, shouting after."
  "Dear, I haven't the knees for mischief. Look elsewhere."
@rule core.accuse.sa_disagree_sad guard: mood=sad act: disagree
  "[SAD]That hurts. I didn't do it. I wouldn't, please believe me."
@rule core.accuse.sa_disagree_angry guard: mood=angry act: disagree
  "[ANGRY]Excuse me? No. Check your facts, then come back, shouting less."
@rule core.accuse.sa_agree act: agree
  "Good point. It does sound like them. I won't say more."
  "I did wonder about that. Funny how things line up."
  "You know, you might be right. It does fit the pattern."
  "Hm. I hadn't thought of it. But now I can't unthink it."
  "I'd keep an eye on that. Quietly. And with snacks."
  "Between us, I had the same feeling. Don't repeat it."
  "That checks out. I saw something odd, and I didn't say."
@rule core.accuse.sa_agree_quirky guard: quirky act: agree
  "Ooh, a mystery! I'll fetch my magnifying glass and my hat."
  "The plot thickens! Like soup, but with more consequences."
@rule core.accuse.sa_agree_friend guard: rel=friend act: agree
  "If you say so, I believe you. You're not one for fibs."
@rule core.accuse.sa_joke act: joke
  "It was the butler. It's always the butler. We haven't got one."
  "I'd like to point out the real culprit: gravity. It started it."
  "An accusation! Quick, dim the lights and cue the organ."
  "Objection, sustained! Overruled! I can't tell, I'm not a judge."
  "In this house we assume innocence and check the cookie jar."
  "Hold the phone. We have a whodunit, and I haven't had lunch."
  "That's the most dramatic thing I've heard today. Do continue."
  "Someone's been at the scones. And by someone, I mean probably me."
@rule core.accuse.sa_joke_night guard: time=night act: joke
  "An accusation after dark? How gothic. Light a candle."
  "At this hour, everyone's a suspect. Even the moon."
@rule core.accuse.sa_joke_flat guard: flat act: joke
  "Gasp, shock. A scandal. That was me being scandalised."
@rule core.accuse.sa_defend act: defend
  "Hang on, they'd never. They're a good egg. A bit cracked, but good."
  "I'll vouch for them. They were with me all afternoon, being dull."
  "Whoa, let's slow down. Let them explain before the pitchforks."
  "That's not fair. They've got a clean record, mostly."
  "I'm sure there's a reasonable answer. Let's ask, nicely."
  "Hey, easy. We don't know the whole story. Nobody ever does."
  "Not them. They can't even steal a biscuit without apologising."
@rule core.accuse.sa_defend_best guard: rel=best act: defend
  "No way. I know them better than I know my own socks."
  "Back off. They're mine to defend, and I'm excellent at it."
@rule core.accuse.sa_defend_polite guard: polite act: defend
  "Surely not. I think we ought to hear their side first."
@rule core.accuse.sa_defend_serious guard: serious act: defend
  "Careful. Accusations stick. Make sure you have your facts."
@rule core.accuse.sa_gossip act: gossip
  "Well, since you ask, I've heard things. Hush hush, mind."
  "Ooh, that fits with what I heard at the baker's."
  "I shouldn't say, but there was a rumour about a hat."
  "Between you and me, the whole street's been saying so."
  "I heard it from someone who heard it from a sheep. Reliable."
  "I couldn't possibly tell you. Come closer, and I will."
  "That reminds me of the bit I heard by the well."
@rule core.accuse.sa_gossip_quirky guard: quirky act: gossip
  "My sources are a crow and a dream. Both agree with you."
@rule core.accuse.sa_gossip_night guard: time=night act: gossip
  "Whispers carry at night. I've heard a few, and they're juicy."
@rule core.accuse.sa_kid_disagree guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: disagree
  "Not me, I didn't do it! I was in the garden! Digging!"
  "Nuh-uh, it was the wind! The wind did it! Ask the wind!"
  "No, I was being good! Ask my teddy! He saw!"
@rule core.accuse.sa_kid_joke guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: joke
  "It was a ghost! A tiny ghost! With a hat, I saw him!"
  "I'd never, I'm an angel! Look at my halo! It's a hula hoop!"
@rule core.accuse.sa_kid_defend guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: defend
  "No fair! They're nice! They shared a cookie once!"
  "Leave them alone! They're my friend! I'll tell on you!"
@rule core.accuse.sa_kid_agree guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: agree
  "Hm, I did see something. It was really suspicious. It had a coat."

# ---- DEFEND: the player stands up for someone -----------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.defend.sa_thank act: thank
  "Thank you for saying so. Nobody ever speaks up. You did."
  "That was kind of you. I'll remember it on a bad day."
  "Cheers, you. That's what a good neighbour does."
  "You stuck up for me! I'm choked up. Don't look."
  "You're too good. Thank you. I'll find a way to repay it."
  "That meant a lot. Properly. I'm not just saying it."
  "Thank you. Back when it matters, you're in my corner."
@rule core.defend.sa_thank_friend guard: rel=friend act: thank
  "Friends do that, don't they? Thank you. I'd do the same."
  "You're a proper pal. I'll bake something. Or buy it."
@rule core.defend.sa_thank_sad guard: mood=sad act: thank
  "[SAD]Thank you. I was feeling small, and you made me bigger."
@rule core.defend.sa_thank_polite guard: polite act: thank
  "How gracious of you. I'm most grateful for the support."
@rule core.defend.sa_thank_elder guard: elder act: thank
  "Bless you, dear. At my age, a friend like you is worth a pension."
@rule core.defend.sa_agree act: agree
  "Exactly. That's what I was going to say, only better."
  "Hear, hear. Well argued. Do it again, louder."
  "You're right. Quite right. I'd have said so sooner."
  "I agree with every word. I've told everyone. They didn't listen."
  "That's it. That's the sensible take. Frame it."
  "Well said. I'm taking notes. Possibly a copy of your speech."
@rule core.defend.sa_agree_topic guard: topic act: agree
  "And as for {x}, that's what I've always said too."
  "Absolutely. And {x} proves it. Case closed."
@rule core.defend.sa_agree_serious guard: serious act: agree
  "I agree. Fairness matters. Let's not rush to judge anyone."
@rule core.defend.sa_agree_blunt guard: blunt act: agree
  "Right. Fine, you're correct. Don't let it go to your head."
@rule core.defend.sa_disagree act: disagree
  "Hm, I'm not sure they deserve it. Have you heard everything?"
  "That's kind, but I'd hold the cheering. There's more to it."
  "I see why you'd say that. I don't quite agree, though."
  "Let's not rush to a hero's welcome. They've got a past."
  "Defend them if you like. I'll keep my own opinions in my pocket."
  "Hm, maybe. But the facts are ticklish, and I'm not convinced."
@rule core.defend.sa_disagree_blunt guard: blunt act: disagree
  "No, they messed up. Own it. Defending isn't fixing."
@rule core.defend.sa_disagree_polite guard: polite act: disagree
  "I appreciate the sentiment, truly. I'm afraid I disagree."
@rule core.defend.sa_joke act: joke
  "My hero! In a cape that doesn't quite fit. Splendid."
  "A defender! Quick, get this person a medal. A small one."
  "You defend them like a lawyer. A tired one, with snacks."
  "Careful. If you keep taking sides, people will start sending you gifts."
  "I'd like to hire you. I've got plenty of arguments. Nobody to win them."
  "Look at us, a defence team. We'd lose, but with style."
  "Right, so we're the good guys. I'll take the cloak with the pockets."
@rule core.defend.sa_joke_flat guard: flat act: joke
  "Ah, a defender. I'd cheer, but my energy's elsewhere. Yay."
@rule core.defend.sa_complain act: complain
  "I'd have liked a defender sooner. It took you a while."
  "Great, now I'm the one in the middle. I hate the middle."
  "It's not fair, being the topic. Why's it always me?"
  "Oh, now they all stare. Thanks. I loved the quiet."
  "I'd rather this was about someone else. Anyone. A tree."
@rule core.defend.sa_complain_tired guard: mood=tired act: complain
  "[SLEEPY]Can we do this tomorrow? I'm too tired for a debate."
@rule core.defend.sa_kid_thank guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: thank
  "Thank you for sticking up for me! You're a superhero!"
  "You said it! Yay! I'll give you my best stick!"
  "That was so nice! I'll draw you a picture. It'll have a dog."
@rule core.defend.sa_kid_joke guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: joke
  "You're the defender! I'm the defendee! That's a word!"
  "My hero! Can I have a cape too? A small cape."
@rule core.defend.sa_kid_agree guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: agree
  "Yeah! What they said! I'd say it too but louder!"
@rule core.defend.sa_kid_complain guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: complain
  "Why's everyone looking at me? I didn't do anything! I think!"

# ---- TAKE_SIDE: the player picks a side ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.take_side.sa_thank act: thank
  "Aw, you're on my side! I've never felt so supported."
  "Thank you for picking me. I know it was a hard choice."
  "That means so much. I'll never forget who stood by me."
  "You've made my day. And my week. And possibly my month."
  "Look at you, taking sides like a champion. Thank you."
  "I'm touched, really. I'd shake your hand but I'm blushing."
  "Thank you. It's good to have someone in the corner, holding the towel."
@rule core.take_side.sa_thank_rival guard: rel=rival act: thank
  "Well, well, you're on my side. That's a first. Don't make it weird."
@rule core.take_side.sa_thank_friend guard: rel=friend act: thank
  "I knew you'd pick me. Not that I was worried. A little worried."
@rule core.take_side.sa_thank_polite guard: polite act: thank
  "How kind of you to say so. I'm deeply obliged."
@rule core.take_side.sa_thank_topic guard: topic act: thank
  "Thank you. And on {x}, we're in total agreement. Brilliant."
@rule core.take_side.sa_agree act: agree
  "Right, so we're a team. I like teams. They have snacks."
  "Same side, then. That's settled. Shake on it, or not."
  "Yes! Finally, a reasonable person. I'd given up hope."
  "Good call. It's the side with the better hats, anyway."
  "Agreed. Let's keep it simple, and a little bit smug."
  "We see things the same way. We should write a pamphlet."
@rule core.take_side.sa_agree_stance guard: stance=pro act: agree
  "You're with me on this? Great. It's a thing worth defending."
@rule core.take_side.sa_agree_stance_con guard: stance=con act: agree
  "Thank goodness. I couldn't stand it, and now I'm not alone."
@rule core.take_side.sa_disagree act: disagree
  "Hm, I'm not sure that's the right side. Think it over."
  "You picked that one? Brave. I'd have picked the other."
  "Well, that's your choice. I respect it. I disagree, loudly."
  "Hold on, you can't just choose. There's a form to fill in."
  "I thought you'd see it my way. Clearly, you saw some other way."
  "Interesting pick. I'll ponder it, and then ignore it."
@rule core.take_side.sa_disagree_blunt guard: blunt act: disagree
  "Wrong side. Switch. I'll wait."
@rule core.take_side.sa_disagree_serious guard: serious act: disagree
  "Think carefully. Choosing a side shapes things. Weigh it up."
@rule core.take_side.sa_complain act: complain
  "Oh, so now it's sides. I was having a nice day, too."
  "I'd hoped you'd stay out of it. It's rarely nice in here."
  "Sides! Everyone's got a side. I'd rather have a sandwich."
  "Great. Now there's two of you against my one good argument."
  "Taking sides splits a room. Look at us. We're a pie chart."
@rule core.take_side.sa_joke act: joke
  "Oh, you've picked a side! Do you get a badge? There should be a badge."
  "I'm on both sides. It's the only way to win with dinner guests."
  "A side! How decisive. I'm still deciding what to have for lunch."
  "You chose well. Or badly. We'll know on Thursday."
  "Sides make a game of it. Do we get a scoreboard?"
  "I'm on the side that has cake. Tell me when that's decided."
  "Ooh, drama. I'll fetch snacks. You two continue."
@rule core.take_side.sa_joke_night guard: time=night act: joke
  "Sides at night. How dramatic. Someone cue the thunder."
@rule core.take_side.sa_joke_flat guard: flat act: joke
  "A side was chosen. I'm moved. This is my moved face."
@rule core.take_side.sa_kid_thank guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: thank
  "Yay, you're on my team! Team, we're a team! Team name: Us!"
  "You picked me! You're the best! I'll draw you a medal!"
@rule core.take_side.sa_kid_agree guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: agree
  "Yeah, same side! We're the winning side! We have a flag!"
@rule core.take_side.sa_kid_complain guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: complain
  "But I wanted you on my side! Why'd you pick that one?"
  "Aww, no fair! Everyone picks the other side! I'm sad!"
@rule core.take_side.sa_kid_joke guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: joke
  "Sides! Left side, right side, tummy side! Which one?"

# ---- MEDIATE: the player tries to calm a row -------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.mediate.sa_agree act: agree
  "You're right. We're being silly. We should talk like grown-ups."
  "Okay, okay. Let's hear it out. I'll even take my coat off."
  "Good idea. A calm word is better than a loud one."
  "Fair. I'll listen first, and then pout, in that order."
  "Yes, let's sort it. We've been at it long enough."
  "You make a decent referee. Would you like a whistle?"
  "Fine, a truce. I'll hold out my hand. A bit."
  "All right. A deep breath, and a fresh start. Here goes."
@rule core.mediate.sa_agree_sad guard: mood=sad act: agree
  "[SAD]Thank you. I didn't want to fight. I just got carried away."
@rule core.mediate.sa_agree_angry guard: mood=angry act: agree
  "[ANGRY]Fine, I'll calm down. Give me a moment. A long moment."
@rule core.mediate.sa_agree_polite guard: polite act: agree
  "Of course. Let's be reasonable. I'm sorry for raising my voice."
@rule core.mediate.sa_agree_friend guard: rel=friend act: agree
  "You always know when to step in. Thank you for being the calm one."
@rule core.mediate.sa_agree_topic guard: topic act: agree
  "Right. Let's put {x} aside. Nobody wins a fight about {x}."
  "Fair. We can talk about {x} later, calmly, with tea."
@rule core.mediate.sa_agree_serious guard: serious act: agree
  "Agreed. We should settle this properly. No shouting, just facts."
@rule core.mediate.sa_agree_elder guard: elder act: agree
  "Wise words, dear. I've seen worse rows over a fence."
@rule core.mediate.sa_disagree act: disagree
  "Stay out of it. This is between us. And possibly a hedge."
  "That's kind, but no. We've got to fight it out. Politely."
  "Peace is nice, but I'm not done being right yet."
  "Hold on. I'll stop when I've said my piece. Maybe two pieces."
  "Calm down? I'm perfectly calm. This is my calm voice."
  "Mediation's a lovely idea. Not today. Today I'm busy."
@rule core.mediate.sa_disagree_blunt guard: blunt act: disagree
  "No, stay out of it. Thanks for the offer. Goodbye."
@rule core.mediate.sa_disagree_angry guard: mood=angry act: disagree
  "[ANGRY]Not now! I'm not finished! Let me finish!"
@rule core.mediate.sa_apologize act: apologize
  "You're right. I overreacted. I'm sorry, to everyone, and the hedge."
  "Sorry. I got hot under the collar. It's a warm collar."
  "I shouldn't have said that. Let me say it nicer."
  "Okay. I'm sorry. I'll make it up with a snack."
  "I was out of line. I'll fix it. Starting with tea."
  "Sorry, all. Peace is better than winning. Mostly."
@rule core.mediate.sa_apologize_polite guard: polite act: apologize
  "I do apologise. It was uncalled for, and I regret it."
@rule core.mediate.sa_apologize_sad guard: mood=sad act: apologize
  "[SAD]I'm sorry. I didn't mean to be unkind. I'll try again."
@rule core.mediate.sa_apologize_elder guard: elder act: apologize
  "Oh, I'm sorry. Old people get cranky. It's in the pension."
@rule core.mediate.sa_joke act: joke
  "Here comes the referee! Make sure you wear stripes."
  "Mediator! Quick, somebody give them a gavel and a bun."
  "Peace talks! I'll bring biscuits. Biscuits end wars."
  "I came for a fight, and I got a counsellor. Not ideal."
  "Look at you, bringing calm. Do you do weddings?"
  "Right, I'll put my fists away. They're not that big anyway."
  "I'll make peace if you pay for lunch. That's the deal."
@rule core.mediate.sa_joke_night guard: time=night act: joke
  "A truce at midnight? How romantic. And how sleepy."
@rule core.mediate.sa_joke_quirky guard: quirky act: joke
  "Peace! Quick, before the spoons start. They're listening."
@rule core.mediate.sa_complain act: complain
  "It's easy to say, calm down. You're not the one who's cross."
  "Oh, the peacemaker's here. How nice. For you."
  "I didn't ask for a mediator. I asked for a chair."
  "Everyone wants peace, until it's their turn to give in."
  "It's not that simple. If it were, I'd have done it by now."
@rule core.mediate.sa_complain_tired guard: mood=tired act: complain
  "[SLEEPY]I'm too tired for this. Can we do it after a nap?"
@rule core.mediate.sa_kid_agree guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: agree
  "Okay, I'm sorry. We can be friends again! With a hug!"
  "Okay, truce! Truce, I'll share my snack! A quarter of it!"
@rule core.mediate.sa_kid_apologize guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: apologize
  "I'm sorry I yelled. I was grumpy. I get hungry grumpy."
  "Sorry! I didn't mean it. I just wanted the red crayon."
@rule core.mediate.sa_kid_disagree guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: disagree
  "No! I'm not done! It's my turn to be right!"
@rule core.mediate.sa_kid_joke guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: joke
  "Peace! Peace and pizza! That's the best peace!"
@rule core.mediate.sa_kid_complain guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: complain
  "It's not my fault! They started it! I only finished it!"
